   "installerTest": "TEST EQUIPMENT section: turn on power. Fan - press the fan button to On (blower starts), then Auto (blower stops immediately); skip if there is no G connection. Heating - press System to Heat (heat pumps: light a standing pilot on the aux system first), raise the setpoint 1 deg above room temperature and the thermostat should indicate 'Heat On'; for heat pumps with auxiliary, raise to 3 deg above room temperature and the display should show 'Heat On Aux'; lower 1 deg below room temperature to stop. Auxiliary (heat pumps with aux only) - press System to Aux, raise 1 deg above room temperature ('Heat On Aux'), then lower 1 deg to stop. Cooling - press System to Cool and lower the setpoint 1 deg below room temperature; the blower should come on immediately at high speed and the display should show 'Cool On' (up to a 5 minute delay if Installer Menu item 50 is On); raise 1 deg above room temperature to stop. Humidity Control check: press Menu 1 second, use Up/Down to reach Settings, press Menu to enter the User Menu, navigate to User Menu item #08 Humidity Control (Hd), use Up/Down to turn it on or off, press Hold/Run to exit.",
   "factoryReset": "Two documented operations. (1) If the thermostat has good batteries but a blank display or does not respond to key presses, reset it by removing the batteries for 2 minutes - this reset does NOT change the menu settings or the program. If the condition persists after reinstalling the batteries, replace the thermostat. (2) To reset only the schedule and user settings back to factory defaults, press the Menu and Backlight buttons at the same time and hold until the display goes blank and resets."
