  "type": "programmable",
  "stages": "1 heat + 1 cool. Configurable as Single Stage 1 (SS1) or Heat Pump 1 (HP1, single stage compressor heat pump with aux/emergency heat). Applications: gas, oil, electric, heat only, cool only or heat/cool, 2- or 3-wire hydronic zone (hot water or steam), 24 v...",
  "sort": 20,
  "confidence": "common",
  "power": {
   "cWire": "optional",
   "batteries": "AA alkaline",
   "notes": "Three power methods selected with the Power Stealing Switches on the rear of the thermostat: (1) battery powered, no 24V system power available - switches On, runs on batteries; (2) hardwired with battery back-up for 24V systems with a common landed on C - switches On, runs on power directly from the transformer with battery back-up; (3) battery powered with Power Stealing Assist for 24V systems with NO common on C - switches On, runs on batteries plus supplemental power drawn through the heat or cool circuit. If Power Stealing Assist is not compatible (draft inducer runs with no call for heat, fan turns on with no call or will not turn off, furnace or A/C will not turn off at the end of a call), move the Power Stealing Switches to Off. C is optional for system operation but required for the remote sensor. Electrical rating: mV to 30 VAC NEC Class II 50/60 Hz or DC; hardwire input 20 to 30 VAC; 1.5 A per terminal, 2.5 A maximum all terminals combined."
  },
