  "wiringNotes": [
   "This thermostat is designed to operate a single-transformer or two-transformer system (Figure 2 single stage/multi-stage; Figure 3 heat pump).",
   "There is no GAS/ELECTRIC slide switch - fan control is Configuration Menu item 2 (GAS = furnace controls the blower, ELE = thermostat controls the blower). G is also energized in heating when configured for Electric heat.",
   "Reversing valve output is Configuration Menu item 3 and only appears when HP1/HP2 is selected: O = energized in Cool and Off; B = energized in Heat and Emergency.",
   "Single-stage 3-wire zone valve applications use terminal 6 (power-closed SPDT connection).",
   "Dual Fuel: with the thermostat in heat pump mode and Dual Fuel selected On, the thermostat either monitors outdoor temperature using remote sensor F145-1378 or uses software logic to decide when to switch to gas heat and shut down the compressor - this eliminates the need for a fossil fuel kit. Compressor shutdown delay (Cd) after aux is energized is 0-99 seconds, default 60.",
   "Remote sensors wire to the +, S and - terminals; C must be powered for remote sensor operation. Indoor and local sensors can be weighted/averaged (A2 average and default, H4 high, L1 low) by pressing Up and Down together while in Set Schedule mode.",
   "Same underlying platform, wiring diagrams and Installer/Configuration Menu structure as the 1F95 Blue Series Touchscreen family (identical Screen Reference numbering, same Comfort Alert diagnostic flash codes, same factory reset combo) - the 1F97 is White-Rodgers' Comfort-Set 90 series branding of this touchscreen platform.",
   "System type (SS1/MS2/HP1/HP2) selected in Installer Configuration Menu item 1 determines terminal function - wire per the correct figure for the selected mode."
  ],
  "setup": {
   "access": "Press the Menu touch key, then press and hold the Installer Config touch key for 5 seconds. This displays screen reference #1. Screen reference numbers appear in the top right corner of the display. Press the right/advance key to go to the next item and the left key to return to a previous item; press Up or Down to change an option. Shaded items are not available when Non-Programmable is selected.",
   "keySettings": [
    {
     "setting": "1 - System type",
     "options": "SS1 (single stage) or HP 1 (heat pump, 1 compressor)",
     "notes": "3-wire zone applications use SS1 (see wiring)"
    },
    {
     "setting": "2 - Fan control (GAS/ELE)",
     "options": "GAS (default) or ELE",
     "notes": "GAS: furnace controls blower. ELE: thermostat controls blower."
    },
    {
     "setting": "3 - Reversing valve (0b)",
     "options": "0 (O, default) or b (B)",
     "notes": "Only appears if HP1 or HP2 is selected"
    },
    {
     "setting": "8 / 9 / 10 - Cycle rates",
     "options": "8 Heat Cr: FA (default) or SL. 9 Cool Cr: FA (default) or SL. 10 Cr/AU Em: FA (default) or SL",
     "notes": "Item 10 only appears if HP1 or HP2 is selected. Rated differentials: Heat FA 0.6 / SL 1.5 deg F; Cool FA 1.2 / SL 1.7; Heat Pump FA 1.2 / SL 1.7; Emer Heat FA 0.6 / SL 1.7"
    },
    {
     "setting": "11 - Stage cycle completion (SC)",
     "options": "OFF (default) or On",
     "notes": ""
    },
    {
     "setting": "12 - Compressor Lockout (CL)",
     "options": "OFF (default) or On",
     "notes": "The setpoint display flashes while the compressor time delay is running"
    },
    {
     "setting": "22 - Compressor Optimization (CO)",
     "options": "Off (default) or On",
     "notes": "Not available on earlier models"
    },
    {
     "setting": "26 / 27 - Keypad Lockout and combination",
     "options": "26: OFF (default), L (total), P (partial), Temperature Limit (limited temperature range). 27: 000 (default) or 001-999",
     "notes": "Forgotten code: press the menu key (the key will disappear) and hold for 20 seconds to unlock"
    },
    {
     "setting": "28 / 29 / 30 - Remote temperature sensor",
     "options": "28 Remote: OFF (default) or On. 29 Remote: In (default) or Outdoor Remote. 30 Local sensor LS: On (default) or OFF",
     "notes": "Local sensor disable is only available when an Indoor Remote is selected On"
    },
    {
     "setting": "31 / 32 / 33 / 34 - Dual Fuel",
     "options": "31 dF: OFF (default) or On (appears if HP1/HP2 selected). 32 dF setpoint with outdoor sensor: 35 default, -5 to 50 deg F. 33 dF setpoint with no outdoor sensor: 05 default, 0 to 09. 34 Cd compressor off delay: 60 default, 0-99 seconds",
     "notes": "Higher temperature or dual fuel number = smaller stage separation (more comfort); lower = larger separation (more economy)"
    },
    {
     "setting": "System Type (Screen Ref 1)",
     "options": "MS2 (default) / HP1 / HP2 / SS1",
     "notes": ""
    },
    {
     "setting": "Fan control (Screen Ref 2)",
     "options": "GAS (default) or ELE",
     "notes": ""
    },
    {
     "setting": "O/B reversing valve (Screen Ref 3)",
     "options": "O (default) or B",
     "notes": "HP1/HP2 only"
    },
    {
     "setting": "Heat/Cool/Aux cycle rate (Screen Ref 8-10)",
     "options": "FA (default) or SL",
     "notes": ""
    },
    {
     "setting": "Compressor Lockout (Screen Ref 12)",
     "options": "OFF (default) or ON",
     "notes": ""
    }
   ],
   "installerTest": "Check Thermostat Operation section. Fan - turn on power, press FAN to ON (blower starts), press FAN to AUTO (blower stops immediately). Heating - press SYSTEM to HEAT (light a standing pilot on the aux system first if present), press Up to 1 deg above room temperature; the display should show 'System On' (a flashing setpoint on HP1 means the 5-minute compressor lockout is running - Configuration menu item 11 per the manual text); raise to 3 deg above room temperature on HP1 and aux heat should run with 'System On +2'; press Down below room temperature to stop. Emergency (heat pumps only) - press SYSTEM to EM, 'EM Heat Mode' flashes, raise the setpoint and the heat source on W/E should run showing 'System On +2' with flashing 'EM Heat Mode' and 'Heat'; lower the setpoint to stop. Cooling - press SYSTEM to Cool and lower the setpoint; the blower should come on immediately on high speed followed by cold air and the display should show 'System On'; raise the setpoint to stop. Do NOT operate cooling if the outdoor temperature is below 50 deg F, and do not run the compressor unless the oil heaters have been operational for 6 hours and the system has been off at least 5 minutes.",
   "factoryReset": "Two documented operations. (1) Installer note in the Configuration Menu: to default the programming, clock and Configuration Menu to the factory default settings, press the Up, Down and SYSTEM keys simultaneously - the display goes blank for a few seconds and then all segments display momentarily. For heat pump systems, Configuration Menu items 1 and 3 must then be re-set to match the heat pump. (2) Reset Operation for a blank/erratic display: remove the thermostat from the wall plate and remove the batteries for 2 minutes, then replace the batteries and re-mount the thermostat."
  },
