   "batteries": "2 AA alkaline (included)",
   "notes": "The thermostat can be powered by system AC power or by battery. If the battery icon is displayed the thermostat is battery powered; if it is not displayed the thermostat is system powered with optional battery back-up. Half-power and 'Change' battery icons are displayed as the batteries deplete. Copeland recommends replacing batteries every 2 years. When less than about two months of battery life remain the setpoint offsets by 10 degrees (10 cooler in Heat / 10 warmer in Cool); the normal setpoint can be manually restored with Up/Down but another offset occurs within two days if the batteries are not replaced. Electrical rating mV to 30 VAC NEC Class II; hardwire input 20 to 30 VAC; 1.5 A per terminal, 2.5 A maximum all terminals combined."
