   "C-Wire Adapter wiring procedure (from the control board side): label and pull G, W/W1 (or O/B on a heat pump), R/Rc, and Y/Y1 at the HVAC board; on the adapter's 'Thermostat' side wire W/O-B -> W, G -> C, R/Rc -> R, Y/Y1 -> K; wire the adapter's 'Equipment' side back to the matching board terminals; at the thermostat itself, relabel/move the G wire into C and the Y wire into K, leaving Y and G empty.",
   "R jumper switch (blue cover, lower right of wall plate): UP position for a single R wire; DOWN position when both R and Rc wires are present.",
   "Before disconnecting anything, photograph the old thermostat's wiring and label each wire with the supplied stickers as it's removed; do not let labeled wires fall back into the wall.",
   "After wiring, verify what the device thinks it sees via Alexa app: Settings > Thermostat Configuration > Connected wire map, and compare to the physical wiring; if they don't match, redo wiring then perform a reset and re-run setup.",
