  "wiringNotes": [
   "Max wire distance thermostat-to-indoor-unit is 125 ft using 18 AWG (min recommended gauge); standard non-stranded thermostat wire is acceptable.",
   "Wiring communicating indoor unit to communicating outdoor unit: connect 1, 2, C, R from the thermostat to 1, 2, R, C at the indoor unit; then connect only wires 1 and 2 from the indoor unit to 1 and 2 at the outdoor unit (do not run R/C to the outdoor unit).",
   "4-pin connectors on communicating indoor/outdoor boards are keyed 1,2,R,C (indoor) and 1,2 (outdoor) - matching pin-for-pin to the thermostat's 1,2,C,R labeling; if wired incorrectly you get a communication error or the equipment is not recognized.",
   "Aux outputs are dry contacts only - a 24VAC+ field control signal must be routed through the contact via a field-supplied SPST relay; the aux terminals used are selected in the installer wizard on the thermostat/app, not fixed by wire color.",
   "Non-communicating (24V conventional) outdoor equipment is only supported by adding a Daikin D24V Gateway (models DTA119A73 current / DTA119A72 legacy) between a Daikin FIT communicating AC or HP + EEV coil and a non-communicating gas furnace of any brand - the Gateway lets the One+ still operate over 1/2/R/C to the FIT system while bridging to the conventional furnace. Daikin's own documentation does not show a direct W/Y/G/O-B conventional terminal set on the One+ itself.",
   "One+ Zoning (Daikin DOZP zone panel): the zone panel's thermostat bus is also 1 (Data 1), 2 (Data 2), C (Common), R (24VAC) - wired the same as a direct thermostat-to-indoor-unit run, just landed at the zone panel instead. Each Daikin One+ zone thermostat draws about 6VA (vs 2.5VA for the zone controller itself and 1.5VA per damper) - include this in the field-supplied 24VAC transformer sizing. On first power-up every wired thermostat defaults to 'additional zone' role; one must be set to 'primary' in Equipment Setup > Zone Board > Thermostat Role, or the indoor unit reports error code E77 and a pop-up nags every wired stat until a primary is chosen. If the primary thermostat doesn't show up in the zone board's 'assign zone devices' list, check the wiring at the thermostat and zone board.",
   "Compatible with the Daikin ONE Wireless RHT Sensor (up to 8 per thermostat, One+ only) for averaged remote temp/humidity sensing without adding a zone or a wired thermostat."
  ],
