  "wiringNotes": [
   "Optional accessories for the CS3000 5/2-day line: outdoor sensor X2658 (used with the 3-stage heat pump model L3532H only) and wall plate X2659. The 1-stage L3511C and 2-stage L3522C have no outdoor sensor terminals.",
   "Do not short (jumper) across terminals on the gas valve or at the system control to test installation - this damages the thermostat and voids the warranty.",
   "Enlarge the wire hole to about 3/4 in by 3/4 in, pull about 3 in of wire through and strip 1/4 in of insulation. After wiring, seal the hole in the wall so unconditioned air in the wall space cannot enter the thermostat.",
   "Do not install on outside walls (unconditioned space on the opposite side) or where direct sunlight can hit the thermostat. Mount about 5 ft above the floor.",
   "Wiring diagrams in 506077-02 cover, for each of L3511C and L3522C: coil blower, coil blower with V drive, furnace, and furnace with V drive. The diagrams are images and were not transcribed.",
   "Heating mode will not operate if the thermostat has been stored or is being used at ambient temperatures above 93 deg F. The heating function is enabled after the thermostat is below 93 deg F for about 30 minutes. (The Merit operation manual describes this as a thermal-mechanical switch that opens W1 - and W2 on the 51M35 - at 93 deg F +/- 6 deg F.)"
  ],
  "setup": {
   "access": "There is no on-screen installer menu. All installer configuration is done with six DIP switches on the back side of the thermostat body (behind the thermostat, accessible with the body removed from the subbase). Use a non-conductive tool and avoid contact with the circuit board and connector prongs.",
   "keySettings": [
    {
     "setting": "DIP 1 - Cal 1 (room temperature offset, 1 deg F)",
     "options": "Off = 0 deg F, On = 1 deg F",
     "notes": "Factory setting Off (0 deg F)"
    },
    {
     "setting": "DIP 2 - Cal 2 (room temperature offset, 2 deg F)",
     "options": "Off = 0 deg F, On = 2 deg F",
     "notes": "Factory setting Off (0 deg F)"
    },
    {
     "setting": "DIP 3 - Cal +/- (offset sign)",
     "options": "Off = Positive, On = Negative",
     "notes": "Factory setting Positive. Combined offsets: Cal1/Cal2/Cal+- = Off/Off/Off is +0, On/Off/Off is +1, Off/On/Off is +2, On/On/Off is +3, Off/Off/On is -0, On/Off/On is -1, Off/On/On is -2, On/On/On is -3 deg F."
    },
    {
     "setting": "DIP 4 - F/C display",
     "options": "Off = Fahrenheit, On = Celsius",
     "notes": "Factory setting Fahrenheit"
    },
    {
     "setting": "DIP 5 - Fan option (heating fan operation)",
     "options": "Off = G (gas), On = E (electric)",
     "notes": "L3511C / L3522C (51M34 / 51M35) only. Factory setting G. Set on G and the furnace controls the fan during heating and the thermostat fan icon is not displayed even though the fan may be energized (gas furnace applications). Set on E and the thermostat controls the fan during heating (electric furnace applications)."
    },
    {
     "setting": "DIP 6 - SSR (Smooth Setback Recovery)",
     "options": "Off = Disable, On = Enable",
     "notes": "Factory setting Disable. When enabled the equipment responds to a program change before the change is set to occur so the setpoint is reached at the event time; disabled, it responds at the programmed time."
    }
   ],
   "installerTest": "",
   "factoryReset": "Press the unlabeled recessed RESET button behind the door on the right-hand side of the thermostat, below the SETTINGS button, using a paper clip or small pencil. ALL settings revert to defaults, including the default program."
  },
