  "wiringNotes": [
   "Two-piece design: Display Module in the living space, Equipment Control Module (relays) near the furnace / fan coil, joined by only 2 wires (V+ and Vg). Single-piece install brings all equipment wiring (up to 14 wires) to the wall. Two-piece is the recommended configuration.",
   "The model numbers on the Display Module and the Equipment Control Module MUST match or behavior is unpredictable. When replacing a failed piece, replace both as a matched set and verify both parts carry the same model and serial number - mixing an AC display with an HP/PAC equipment control module makes some setup options appear and others disappear, which is very confusing to troubleshoot.",
   "All wiring 22 AWG or larger; continuous runs over 100 ft (30.5 m) use 20 AWG or larger; no run over 250 ft (76 m).",
   "Do NOT hang the Display Module from the Equipment Control Module screw terminals - the 2-wire pigtail is not rated to hold its weight.",
   "Do not mount the Equipment Control Module on ductwork, or below any other control or equipment (humidistat, humidifier, etc).",
   "Never remove the thermostat board from its plastic housing - it can warp and damage the board.",
   "No part of the control may be installed outdoors or in an outdoor cabinet.",
   "Coil a service loop of excess wire behind the mounting plate to keep strain off the terminal strip, and seal the wall hole - drafts cause false temperature readings.",
   "Split-power (2 transformer) hookup: 'NOTE: Rc/Rh jumper is cut on the Equipment Control Module' - see Fig. 26 single-stage furnace with AC and split power.",
   "This thermostat uses LATCHING relays. On loss of power the relays stay in their last position, so straight out of the box outputs may read as ON with the stat unpowered. That is normal; only check output states with the thermostat powered.",
   "On power up all segments light for 5 sec, then a 2-digit configuration code appears for 5 sec: AC = 1-stage AC, HP = 1-stage heat pump, H = heat only, C = cool only, H2 = 2-stage heat pump with fan coil, A2 = 2-stage AC with fan coil or furnace (see Option 33/01)."
  ],
  "setup": {
   "access": "Press and hold the FAN button for approximately 10 seconds to enter Configuration Mode. Option number shows in the heat-setpoint position, setting in the cool-setpoint position. On programmable (TP-PAC/PHP) models a box surrounds the active value - MODE or the soft keys move the box, UP/DOWN change it. On non-programmable (TP-NAC/NHP) models the active value FLASHES - MODE or the Home/Sleep keys change which value flashes. Changes save at the moment of selection. Auto-exits after 3 minutes with no button press; FAN or DONE exits immediately.",
   "keySettings": [
    {
     "setting": "Option 01 - Equipment Type",
     "options": "HP model: HP, AC, H, C, H2, A2. AC model: AC, H, C",
     "notes": "HP = 1-speed heat pump with fan coil; AC = 1-speed AC; H = heat only, no outdoor unit; C = cool only, fan coil with no strip heat; A2 = 2-stage AC with furnace or fan coil; H2 = 2-stage heat pump with fan coil. Default HP on the HP model, AC on the AC model."
    },
    {
     "setting": "Option 04 - Fan (G) on with W/W1",
     "options": "On or OF, default OF",
     "notes": "Most furnaces and fan coils run their own blower - leave OF. Set On only if the auxiliary heater needs a separate G signal."
    },
    {
     "setting": "Option 10 - Reversing Valve",
     "options": "H or C, default C",
     "notes": "C = O/W2/B energized in COOL (standard Carrier O logic). H = energized in HEAT (B logic). Heat pump systems only. Defrost detection does not work properly if configured as B."
    },
    {
     "setting": "Option 32 - Furnace Heat Staging",
     "options": "1 or 2, default 1",
     "notes": "Only when the HP thermostat is configured for AC equipment or Heat Only. 1 = thermostat drives W1 only, furnace stages itself. 2 = thermostat drives W1 and O/W2/B."
    },
    {
     "setting": "Option 33 - Single or Two-Piece Installation",
     "options": "1P or 2P, default 2P",
     "notes": "Sets the self-heat compensation applied to the temperature sensor. Set it to match how the unit was actually mounted."
    },
    {
     "setting": "Option 41 - Variable Speed Blower",
     "options": "On or OF, default OF",
     "notes": "OF = single speed (PSC) blower, On = variable speed. Enables Option 44."
    },
    {
     "setting": "Option 16 - Maximum Cycles Per Hour",
     "options": "2, 4 or 6, default 4",
     "notes": "2 = 30 min lockout between starts, 4 = 15 min, 6 = 10 min."
    },
    {
     "setting": "Option 17 - Time Between Equipment Stages",
     "options": "10, 15, 20, 25 minutes, default 15",
     "notes": "Heat pump systems only - minutes on the highest compressor stage before auxiliary heat is allowed. Staging between speeds inside one piece of equipment is fixed at 10 minutes."
    },
    {
     "setting": "Option 11 - Deadband Between Heat and Cool",
     "options": "1 to 6 deg, default 2",
     "notes": "Not available on heat-only or cool-only. Also sets the range limits of Options 26 and 27."
    },
    {
     "setting": "Option 05 - Room Air Temperature Sensing",
     "options": "L (local), r (remote), Lr (average), default L",
     "notes": "Programmable models only. Multiple remote sensors can be averaged with series-parallel wiring."
    },
    {
     "setting": "Option 08 - Auxiliary Heat Lockout Temperature",
     "options": "OF, or 5 to 55 deg F in 5 deg steps, default OF",
     "notes": "Heat pump plus valid OAT sensor only. Outdoor temp ABOVE which aux heat is not allowed (unless EM HEAT is selected). Aux is still allowed if room temp falls below 45 deg F."
    },
    {
     "setting": "Option 06 - Cooling Lockout Below 55 deg F",
     "options": "On or OF, default OF",
     "notes": "Requires an OAT sensor; the option is hidden without one."
    },
    {
     "setting": "Option 07 - Zoning",
     "options": "On or OF, default OF",
     "notes": "Set On when the stat is part of a zoning system - the zone panel then handles time guard and cycle timers; the thermostat still enforces minimum on-time."
    },
    {
     "setting": "Option 03 - Fahrenheit / Centigrade",
     "options": "F or C, default F",
     "notes": "Homeowner-accessible."
    },
    {
     "setting": "Option 21 - Keypad Lockout",
     "options": "Programmable: OF, 1 (setpoints + time), 2 (setpoints only), 3 (fully locked). Non-programmable: OF, 1 (setpoints), 2 (fully locked). Default OF",
     "notes": "Padlock icon shows when locked. Unlock by holding UP and DOWN together for 5 seconds; re-locks after 2 minutes with no button press. Never locks while in configuration or installer test mode."
    }
   ],
   "installerTest": "Press and hold FAN for 15 seconds (10 sec gets you Configuration Mode - keep holding through 15 sec for Installer Test Mode). MODE changes the operating mode being tested; AUTO is not available in test. HEAT: stage 1 for 3 minutes, then stages 1+2 for another 3 minutes, with a 180-to-0 second countdown per stage on the display; HEAT ON icon shows, and the auxiliary-heat-on icon shows if stage 2 is electric heat on an HP configuration. COOL: same sequence with COOL ON displayed. On a heat pump with the mode set to EM HEAT the auxiliary heat runs 3 minutes with the clock counting 180 to 0. FAN button toggles the FAN icon between AUTO and On, energizing G (some fan coils keep the fan running 90 sec after G drops). Test terminates after 15 minutes of no button presses; DONE exits immediately. Change MODE to OFF to end a stage test early.",
   "factoryReset": "Option 99 - Reset to Factory Defaults. Enter configuration mode, select Option 99; 99 shows on the left and 10 on the right. Use MODE to move the box to (or flash) the 10, then press and HOLD the DOWN key. The 10 counts down to zero; hold until it reaches zero and the reset executes. At zero the heat setpoint shows '- -', the cool setpoint shows '-' and the room temperature shows 'Fd'. The stat then behaves as if power was cycled. Releasing DOWN early returns the value to 10 and cancels the reset. WARNING: all configuration, program, clock and calendar settings are lost."
  },
