  "wiringNotes": [
   "TSTAT-3W wiring note 2: to activate the dehumidify function on FK or FV series fan coils, remove the J1 jumper at the fan coil control board.",
   "TSTAT-3W wiring note 18: remove the DE jumper to enable the DEHUM input on the furnace control board.",
   "TSTAT-3W wiring note 12: on a current-style variable-speed 80 percent non-condensing furnace, disconnect the green (DEHUM) wire from G on the furnace control board and connect it to the dehumidify terminal on the Thermidistat Control.",
   "TSTAT-3W wiring note 11: on older-style variable-speed furnaces without a DE connection (Carrier 58MVP), a pilot-duty 24 VAC relay must be used to activate the dehumidify feature.",
   "TSTAT-3W wiring note 19: no connection should be made to the furnace HUM terminal.",
   "TSTAT-3W wiring note 3: the heat pump must have a high pressure switch for dual fuel applications.",
   "TSTAT-3W wiring note 9: an outdoor air sensor must be attached in all dual fuel applications.",
   "TSTAT-3W wiring note 17: Configuration Option No. 10 (Dual Fuel Selection) must be turned ON in all dual fuel applications.",
   "TSTAT-3W wiring notes 13-16 (outdoor unit DIP switches): DIP switch 1 OFF for air conditioner installations (factory default), DIP switch 1 ON for heat pump installations; DIP switch 2 OFF for single-speed compressor (factory default), DIP switch 2 ON for 2-speed compressor.",
   "TSTAT-3W wiring note 5: select the zone position on the 2-speed heat pump control board - applies to 38YDA (R-22) units only.",
   "TSTAT-3W wiring note 8: the furnace must control its own second-stage heat operation via its own control algorithm."
  ],
