  "wiringNotes": [
   "This is a fully communicating (non-conventional) control: only 4 wires (A+, R, C, B-) run between the thermostat, outdoor unit, and indoor unit - there is no W/Y/G/O wiring at the thermostat itself.",
   "Each S1-TTSCC01 kit includes a Communicating Plug Harness for the OUTDOOR unit: disconnect all power, remove the factory low-voltage harness, plug the communicating harness into the outdoor control's communication port, then wire-nut the thermostat's 4 wires (A+, R, C, B-) to the harness leads matching color/letter, and route the wire-nutted joints into the outdoor control's junction box.",
   "INDOOR unit (communicating furnace/air handler, denoted by a '-C' in the model number) is wired via screw terminals: 4 wires from the thermostat plus 4 from the outdoor control land on 8 screw terminals total, matched A+ = A+, R = R, C = C, B- = B-; wire nuts may be used outside the unit if the screw terminals are hard to reach. The furnace control may print GND in place of C.",
   "Required hard jumpers that will flag an installation error if wrong: outdoor unit - Fossil Fuel vs Hot Heat Pump (heat pump/AC units only, no jumper needed on straight AC); indoor unit - Heat/No Heat, AC/HP, and Hum Stat (Hum Stat jumper on an AHV/AV/MV air handler must be set to YES for humidifier operation). Other jumpers can be set later from the thermostat but installers should still set them correctly at the equipment to avoid confusion during future service.",
   "For a non-communicating outdoor or indoor unit paired with the S1-TTSCC01, use a Communicating Interface Control Field Kit (S1-33102953000) to convert communicating commands to conventional 24VAC W/Y/G/O outputs; a communicating variable-speed modulating furnace can also directly relay 24VAC outputs to a non-communicating air conditioner.",
   "Bypass and fan-powered humidifiers are wired from the furnace/air handler's own R/G/Y/Y2/W1/W2/O/HUM/X/L/COM terminals (not from the thermostat) - do NOT use a traditional humidistat; the Touch Screen Communicating Control operates the humidifier directly once added via Edit/Add Devices.",
   "A separate 'System Wiring Diagrams' document (036-23098-001-B-0312) contains a full numbered cross-reference (System ID, e.g. HP1-HP40+, AC-series, FC-series) of every supported indoor/outdoor equipment combination with heat-kit staging notes - the thermostat displays its detected System ID (e.g. 'AC15', 'HP14') on the Auto Setup and Edit/Add Devices screens for cross-checking against that table.",
   "Mini-USB port (with included USB-A adapter, S1-03102965000) on the bottom of the unit is used to import/export Program Schedule, Dealer Information, Dealer Logo, Homeowner Configuration, and full Installer Configuration files."
  ],
  "setup": {
   "access": "Press and hold the brand logo (upper right of the home screen) for 5 seconds to enter Service Mode (gray background). On initial power-up the control automatically walks the installer through Auto Setup instead (date/time, software revision, a 1-10 second network listen, system discovery, then Mode selection: System Master / Demo / Service Tool).",
   "keySettings": [
    {
     "setting": "Control Mode",
     "options": "System Master, Demo Mode, Service Tool Mode",
     "notes": "Set on first power-up (Screen 5); System Master = normal residential install; Service Tool Mode only views a system already run by another master control"
    },
    {
     "setting": "Heat Kit Configuration",
     "options": "model-specific heat kit list + 1st/2nd stage kW",
     "notes": "Appears only with a communicating variable-speed air handler (-C model) that has its heat-kit jumper set to Heat; must match the physically installed heat kit or airflow/limit trips can occur"
    },
    {
     "setting": "System ID",
     "options": "e.g. AC-series, HP1-HP40+, FC-series (auto-detected)",
     "notes": "Auto-discovered from attached equipment; installer presses Accept or Re-configure; cross-reference in doc 036-23098-001-B-0312"
    },
    {
     "setting": "Heat Pump Config - Compressor Delay",
     "options": "ON/OFF",
     "notes": "Holds compressor off 30 sec after reversing valve energizes in defrost, to reduce noise"
    },
    {
     "setting": "Heat Pump Config - Defrost Curve",
     "options": "1-6",
     "notes": "Factory set; change only when installing a repair part"
    },
    {
     "setting": "Heat Pump Config - Switch Point",
     "options": "35, 40, 45 deg F",
     "notes": "Liquid-line sensor temp at which the heat pump is forced to 2nd stage"
    },
    {
     "setting": "Heat Pump Config - Y2 Lock",
     "options": "ON/OFF",
     "notes": "Allows anticipation of 2nd-stage operation; must be OFF for the Auxiliary Switch 'Stage Down' function"
    },
    {
     "setting": "Balance Point / Low Temp Cutout (LTCO)",
     "options": "outdoor temp thresholds",
     "notes": "Above balance point = heat pump only; below LTCO = aux/fossil heat only; between the two = staged; if a heating call is unsatisfied after 4 hours aux heat is added automatically"
    },
    {
     "setting": "Airflow Configuration - Delay Profile",
     "options": "Dry, Temperate, Humid, Normal",
     "notes": "Cooling-only airflow ramp-down profile; on a variable-speed communicating indoor unit"
    },
    {
     "setting": "Airflow Configuration (High/Low Cool, High/Low Heat)",
     "options": "CFM in 10 CFM steps, min 400 / max 1800 shown as example",
     "notes": "Restore Defaults button returns airflow to factory CFM"
    },
    {
     "setting": "Float Switch Installed / Shutdown action",
     "options": "Yes/Not Available; Shutdown on Open or Closed",
     "notes": "Condensate float switch behavior"
    },
    {
     "setting": "Auxiliary Switch action (heating/cooling)",
     "options": "No Action, Stage Down, Turn off Compressor (switch to backup heat)",
     "notes": "Default = No Action; Stage Down requires Y2 Lock OFF"
    },
    {
     "setting": "User Interface Settings (homeowner restrictions)",
     "options": "Yes/No per item: Fan icon/status, Humidity icon/status, Outdoor temp display, Upgrade Firmware, Import/Export config, New/View log entries, Enable Security",
     "notes": "Installer controls what the homeowner can see/do"
    },
    {
     "setting": "Edit/Add Devices",
     "options": "Furnace, Heat Pump, Humidifier, EAC, UV Lamp, Ventilator (Generic/ERV/HRV)",
     "notes": "Accessories must be added here for the control to manage or maintenance-track them; a control reset may be needed after removing a device"
    }
   ],
   "installerTest": "Service Mode > Menu > Forced Operation. Three modes: Cool Mode (1st/2nd stage cooling, continuous fan), Heat Mode (heat pump compressor heat if present, furnace/gas heat, electric/air-handler heat), IAQ Mode (added IAQ accessories, may need an ERV/HRV interface control). Select a mode, set a run time (bypassable any time with Stop), select the specific operation and press Apply; optional modifiers (Bypass ASCD, Set Airflow) can be layered on. Forced operation suspends normal setpoint/schedule control system-wide until Exit is pressed; from System Map during a forced test the installer can still view Equipment Details/Status/Inputs-Outputs and the fault Log.",
   "factoryReset": "Service Mode > Menu > Tools/Settings > Administrator Tools > Restore Defaults. This returns the control to factory settings and re-runs the Auto Setup screens on reboot; used after a hard-jumper change or equipment swap causes a System Misconfiguration. Administrator Tools also offers Restart Firmware (simulates a power loss / re-validates settings without erasing them) and Firmware update via USB (a firmware flash DOES restore defaults - export the Installer Configuration file first so it can be re-imported after flashing)."
  },
